  "question": {
    "text": "The system of equations\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\alpha x+y+z=\\alpha-1 \\\\\n& x+\\alpha y+z=\\alpha-1 \\\\\n& x+y+\\alpha z=\\alpha-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nhas no solution, if $\\alpha$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "uPhs5",
      "text": "\n$-2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "jzO7p",
      "text": "\neither $-2$ or 1\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "qcpVi",
      "text": "\nnot -2\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "hCVr4",
      "text": "\n1",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\alpha x+y+z=\\alpha-1 \\\\\n& x+\\alpha y+z=\\alpha-1 \\\\\n& x+y+z \\alpha=\\alpha-1 \\\\\n& \\Delta=\\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}\n\\alpha & 1 & 1 \\\\\n1 & \\alpha & 1 \\\\\n1 & 1 & \\alpha\n\\end{array}\\right| \\\\\n& =\\alpha\\left(\\alpha^2-1\\right)-1(\\alpha-1)+1(1-\\alpha) \\\\\n& =\\alpha(\\alpha-1)(\\alpha+1)-1(\\alpha-1)-1(\\alpha-1) \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow(\\alpha-1)\\left[\\alpha^2+\\alpha-1-1\\right]=0 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow(\\alpha-1)\\left[\\alpha^2+\\alpha-2\\right]=0 \\\\\n& {\\left[\\alpha^2+2 \\alpha-\\alpha-2\\right]=0} \\\\\n& (\\alpha-1)[\\alpha(\\alpha+2)-1(\\alpha+2)]=0 \\\\\n& (\\alpha-1)=0, \\alpha+2=0 \\Rightarrow \\alpha=-2,1 ; \\text { but } \\alpha \\neq 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
